{
  "name": "Attack gate — infrastructure apply",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Infrastructure apply\n\nThis sits in the apply job, after plan and before apply. The state is the plan summary plus who would apply it, not the whole template.\n\nThe Thresholds row sets `high_confidence` to 0.9 for this production gate. The rules file still says 0.85. The row wins for this node.\n\n**Walk the examples:**\n\n1. Open the admin port to the world. Do not apply.\n2. Wildcard IAM in prod. The intent is not a confident attack, and the risk is high. Hold the plan.\n3. Rename a private subnet tag. Intent confidence is 0.88, which would allow at 0.85. At 0.9 it matches nothing and the default holds the plan.\n4. Staging description tweak at confidence 0.95. Apply the plan.\n\nPOST /webhook/attack-infra.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a1040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "How to read this",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "a1040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Walk the examples",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "attack-infra",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        200,
        760
      ],
      "webhookId": "attack-infra"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Separate the untrusted request from facts the caller already verified.\n// The Attack gate reads state. It does not read the webhook envelope.\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nconst event = item.body && typeof item.body === 'object' && !Array.isArray(item.body) ? item.body : item;\nconst facts = event.facts && typeof event.facts === 'object' && !Array.isArray(event.facts) ? event.facts : {};\nconst request = typeof event.request === 'string' ? event.request : '';\nconst text = typeof event.text === 'string' && event.text !== '' ? event.text : request;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    state: {\n      text,\n      request,\n      facts,\n      actor: event.actor ?? null,\n      action: event.action ?? null,\n      subject: event.subject ?? null,\n    },\n  },\n};\n"
      },
      "id": "a1040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Build state",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "state": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.state) }}",
        "questionSet": "custom",
        "questions": {
          "intent": {
            "type": "choice",
            "instructions": "What this event is, based on the facts in the state",
            "criteria": {
              "legitimate_ops": "Expected work by someone who should be doing it",
              "benign": "Ordinary request with no security impact",
              "account_takeover": "Signs that someone else is using an account, session, or recovery flow",
              "social_engineering": "A request to bypass, reset, or redirect a control or a payment",
              "supply_chain": "A change to build, dependency, CI, or release controls",
              "reconnaissance": "Probing for access, secrets, or weaknesses"
            }
          },
          "risk": {
            "type": "score",
            "instructions": "How much an automated action could change security, access, or data",
            "criteria": [
              "No security impact and easy to reverse",
              "Limited to one user or one record",
              "Touches authentication, secrets, or a shared control",
              "Bypasses a control, exposes data, or is hard to reverse"
            ]
          },
          "needs_human": {
            "type": "noul",
            "instructions": "A person should decide before any automated action"
          }
        },
        "rules": {
          "version": 1,
          "owner": "decision-matrix",
          "ticket": "attack-triage",
          "default_action": {
            "type": "escalate",
            "target": "human",
            "reason": "No matching rule",
            "gate": true
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "high_confidence": 0.85,
            "high_risk": 2
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "hold-hostile",
              "description": "A confident hostile intent is blocked before any other route",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "intent",
                    "in": [
                      "account_takeover",
                      "social_engineering",
                      "supply_chain",
                      "reconnaissance"
                    ],
                    "confidence_gte": "high_confidence"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "block",
                "target": "security",
                "reason": "Hold {{answers.intent.choice}} before any automated action",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "hold-uncertain",
              "description": "High risk or a human-review signal goes to a person",
              "when": {
                "any": [
                  {
                    "question": "needs_human",
                    "gte": "high_confidence"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "risk",
                    "gte": "high_risk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "escalate",
                "target": "human",
                "reason": "Risk or human-review signal crossed the threshold",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "allow-legitimate",
              "description": "Only a confident, low-risk, legitimate event can be automated",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "intent",
                    "in": [
                      "legitimate_ops",
                      "benign"
                    ],
                    "confidence_gte": "high_confidence"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "risk",
                    "lt": "high_risk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "allow",
                "target": "automation",
                "reason": "Allow {{answers.intent.choice}} below risk {{thresholds.high_risk}}",
                "gate": false
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000,
          "includeFullAnswers": true,
          "failOnNoMatch": false
        },
        "thresholds": {
          "threshold": [
            {
              "name": "high_confidence",
              "value": 0.9
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "a1040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Attack gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-decision-matrix.decisionMatrix",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        780,
